      "message": "Could we leave hook-denied flows unclassified here? `cnat_hook_deny()` sets the canonical rewrite\u0027s next node to `DROP` and clears its `ts_rw_bm` bit. An NPOL deny therefore reaches this branch with neither bitmap bit set and increments `/cnat/flows/pass-through`, although failed flows should contribute only to `total`. Please check the drop sentinel before classifying an empty bitmap as pass-through, or preserve an explicit denied state. Could we also add inbound and outbound NPOL-deny coverage asserting all class gauges remain zero?",
